---
title: Chicken Karaage
servings: 4
course: dinner
cuisine: Japanese
tags: chicken, fried
image: https://www.themealdb.com/images/media/meals/tyywsw1505930373.jpg
source: https://norecipes.com/karaage-recipe
---

Add the @ginger{1%tbsp}, @garlic{1%clove}, @soy sauce{2%tbsp}, @sake{1%tbsp} and @sugar{2%tsp} to a #bowl{} and whisk to combine. Add the @chicken thigh{450%g}(boneless, skin-on), then stir to coat evenly. Cover and refrigerate for at least ~{1%hour}.

Add 1 inch of @vegetable oil{80%ml} to a heavy bottomed #pot{} and heat until the oil reaches 360 degrees F. Line a wire rack with 2 sheets of paper towels and get your #tongs{} out. Put the @potato starch{80%ml} in a #bowl{}.

Add a handful of chicken to the potato starch and toss to coat each piece evenly.

Fry the karaage in batches until the exterior is a medium brown and the chicken is cooked through. Transfer the fried chicken to the paper towel lined rack. If you want the karaage to stay crispy longer, you can fry the chicken a second time, until it's a darker color after it's cooled off once. Serve with @lemon{80%ml}(wedges).
